{# ------------------------------------------------------------------ #}
{# ObscuraLens Markdown report template (v5.1)                         #}
{#                                                                      #}
{# Context contract (shared with standalone_report.html.j2):           #}
{#   sections: [{'title': str,                                          #}
{#               'rows': [[cell, ...], ...],   # first row = header     #}
{#               'notes': str (optional)}]                              #}
{#   meta:     {'title', 'target', 'kind', 'version', 'generated',      #}
{#              'channel', 'band', 'score', 'top_signals'}              #}
{#                                                                      #}
{# Markdown is rendered with trim_blocks/lstrip_blocks, so control      #}
{# lines never leak into the output. Cell values are piped through the  #}
{# `cell` macro which escapes pipe characters so tables can never       #}
{# break, and collapses newlines (Markdown table rows are single-line). #}
{#- ------------------------------------------------------------------ -#}

{#- cell(value): one table cell, safe for Markdown pipe tables -#}
{% macro cell(value) -%}
{{- value|replace('|', '\\|')|replace('\n', ' ')|replace('\r', ' ') -}}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- row(cells): a full `| a | b |` table line -#}
{% macro row(cells) -%}
| {% for entry in cells %}{{ cell(entry) }}{% if not loop.last %} | {% endif %}{% endfor %} |
{%- endmacro %}

{#- separator(count): the `| --- | --- |` alignment line -#}
{% macro separator(count) -%}
|{% for _ in range(count) %} --- |{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

{#- table(section): the pipe table for one section (header = rows[0]) -#}
{% macro table(section) -%}
{% if section.rows %}
{{ row(section.rows[0]) }}
{{ separator(section.rows[0]|length) }}
{% for line in section.rows[1:] %}
{{ row(line) }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
_(no rows collected)_
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}

# {{ meta.title }}

**ObscuraLens OSINT report**{% if meta.kind %} · kind: `{{ meta.kind }}`{% endif %}{% if meta.channel %} · channel: `{{ meta.channel }}`{% endif +%}

{# Build the meta bullets with list-append expressions: block tags are
   fully trimmed, so each rendered bullet keeps exactly one newline. #}
{% set bullets = [] %}
{% if meta.target %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('- **Target:** `' ~ meta.target ~ '`') %}
{% endif %}
{% if meta.band %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('- **Risk band:** **' ~ meta.band ~ '**'
                          ~ (' (rule score ' ~ meta.score ~ '/100)'
                             if meta.score is defined and meta.score is not none
                             else '')) %}
{% endif %}
{% if meta.top_signals %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('- **Top signals:**') %}
{% for signal in meta.top_signals %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('  - ' ~ signal|replace('\n', ' ')) %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('- **Generated:** ' ~ (meta.generated|fmt_date)) %}
{% set _ = bullets.append('- **Engine:** ObscuraLens v' ~ meta.version) %}
{% for bullet in bullets %}
{{ bullet }}
{% endfor %}

---

{% if sections %}
## Contents

{% for section in sections %}
{{ loop.index }}. [{{ section.title }}](#{{ section.title|lower|replace(' ', '-') }})
{% endfor %}

---
{% endif %}

{% for section in sections %}
## {{ section.title }}

{{ table(section) }}

{% if section.notes %}
> {{ section.notes|replace('\n', '\n> ') }}
{% endif %}

{% else %}
## No sections

This report contains no data sections. Either the underlying lookup
returned no fields or the report was rendered from an empty run.
{% endfor %}

---

## About this report

Scores and bands summarise weighted rule hits over the collected fields
(`clean` < 10, `watch` 10-29, `elevated` 30-59, `high` 60-79,
`critical` 80+). Every rule describes a technical indicator only --
heuristics for analysts, not evidence and not verdicts about people.

*Generated by ObscuraLens v{{ meta.version }} on {{ meta.generated|fmt_date }}.
Data was collected from public sources at a point in time and may be
stale or wrong; verify anything material independently before acting.*
